@api = http://localhost:5080

### USB install check
GET {{api}}/api/incidents/search?q=USB

### T-01 valid create (expect 201, CreatedIncidentResponse, Location header)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "  Lab2 valid incident  ",
  "description": "Valid description for the create check.",
  "severity": "low",
  "occurredAtUtc": "2026-10-10T10:00:00Z"
}

### T-02a severity "7" (expect 400, key severity)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lab2 severity seven",
  "description": "Valid description for the severity check.",
  "severity": "7",
  "occurredAtUtc": "2026-10-10T10:00:00Z"
}

### T-02b several errors at once (expect 400: title, description, severity)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   ",
  "description": "",
  "severity": "Nope",
  "occurredAtUtc": "2026-10-10T10:00:00Z"
}

### T-02c missing occurredAtUtc (expect 400, key occurredAtUtc)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lab2 missing date",
  "description": "Valid description for the date check.",
  "severity": "Low"
}

### T-02d date more than 5 min in future (expect 400, key occurredAtUtc)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lab2 future date",
  "description": "Valid description for the date check.",
  "severity": "Low",
  "occurredAtUtc": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### Offset date accepted (expect 201, stored as UTC)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lab2 offset date",
  "description": "Valid description for the offset check.",
  "severity": "Medium",
  "occurredAtUtc": "2026-10-10T13:00:00+03:00"
}

### T-09a High with 39 chars (expect 400, key description)
POST {{api}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

